  "description": "EPUFEC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H91 Dy7 N24 O34 P4,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.572-4.129 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.12-117.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy7(eddc)2(spch)2(O3PC10H7)4(OAc)5(MeOH)4]·4MeOH (C106H107Dy7N24O38P4). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 5 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
